    "body": "Bisect on a Linux host (debug, `cargo test -p camcraft-app`):\n\n1. **`microarc_test_part::a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a` - caused by #2386.** Green at `e87658f44` (#2068 merge), red at `b25aae66a` (#2386 merge), still red on main `7bcc13a4b`. Assert text: `tests/golden/nc/tormach/wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc: line count 3246 != 3245`. One more posted line than the golden; it must be checked whether that line is correct before the golden moves.\n2. **New since this issue: `stock_source_holes::framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number` - caused by #2450.** Green at `3e5d1cc7f` (#2420 merge), red at `7bcc13a4b` (#2450 merge). The generate step now refuses: `the edge near X35.000 Y1.750 has no wall under it down to the chamfer's depth Z19.000 - a 1 mm chamfer there would ride into the part`. #2450's new chamfer-edge law now refuses this fixture before the test reaches the refusal it pins; the fixture or the law must be read, not the assertion relaxed.\n3. `ui guide_projects::demo_projects_build_and_load_with_valid_paths` was not reproduced here.\n\nBoth #2386 and #2450 are mkinney's PRs, so mkinney's agents take this (claim below). The maintainer can take it back at any time.\n",
